title: The Coup
subtitle: An armed attempt against the government; PPS decides its stance and the part of its organisations.
new-page: true
tags: pl_event
face-image: img/polish/polish_event_coup.jpg
view-if: {! return !!Q.S && !!Q.polish_security_rules && PolishSecurity.coupDue(Q) !}
on-arrival: {!
// Event coup.attempt (technical reference 16.4–16.8, 19.1; card catalogue 9.15; profile coup_f_v1 of M08): the
// sequence F3, F4, F5, F6+F7, F9 only with a significant share of PPS, and F10+F11. No month is spent; the four
// rounds are computed by the engine, without menus of routes, units or tasks. The army groups are synthetic; they
// follow the pattern of May 1926 recorded in HISTORICAL_SOURCES.md, not its units and numbers (stage 8, 8f).
PolishSecurity.coupView(Q);
!}
go-to: f3 if pl_coup_step = "f3"; f4 if pl_coup_step = "f4"; f5 if pl_coup_step = "f5"; f67 if pl_coup_step = "f67"; f9 if pl_coup_step = "f9"; f10 if pl_coup_step = "f10"

@f3
new-page: true

= An attempt against the government

Units close to Józef Piłsudski march on the capital; the government refuses to step down. The pressure towards a coup has passed every threshold of the attempt. The army groups of this game are a synthetic profile, not the units of May 1926.

What PPS knows of the loyalty of the groups to Piłsudski is only an interval: [+ pl_coup_known +]. Democracy stands at [+ pl_coup_democracy +]; it shifts how many soldiers are ready to join. No month is spent until the attempt is resolved.

- @begin: Decide the stance of PPS.

@begin
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupBegin(Q);
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f4
new-page: true

= The stance of PPS

The factions react to the stance as soon as it is confirmed; a faction whose dissent reaches 60 may leave in part when the attempt is over.

- @support_pils
- @defend_legal
- @mediate

@support_pils
title: Support Piłsudski
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_support_pils_preview +]. The relation with Piłsudski improves at the end (+4, and +4 more for an executed share); the parties of the attacked cabinet the opposite.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'support_pils').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'support_pils');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@defend_legal
title: Defend the legal government
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_defend_legal_preview +]. The relation with Piłsudski worsens at the end (−4, and −4 more for an executed share); the parties of the attacked cabinet the opposite.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'defend_legal').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'defend_legal');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@mediate
title: Stay neutral
subtitle: Factions: [+ pl_coup_mediate_preview +]. No change of relations; the Milicja may only protect our own people.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupStanceStatus(Q, 'mediate').available !}
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStance(Q, 'mediate');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f5
new-page: true

= The organisations of PPS

We call our organisations; how many answer depends on their readiness and discipline, not on this choice alone. Milicja: [+ pl_coup_militia_forecast +]. Railways: [+ pl_coup_rail_forecast +]. A strike delays only the rail transports of the side we oppose, and only when enough workers keep it up in the round before a transport arrives.

- @commit_none
- @commit_rail
- @commit_militia
- @commit_both

@commit_none
title: Do not engage our organisations
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'none');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_rail
title: Call the railway workers to strike
subtitle: A quarter of a month's cost of the strike per round from the fund of the railway branch.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'rail').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_rail_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'rail');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_militia
title: Call the Milicja
subtitle: One task: to fight on the side we support, or, if we stay neutral, to protect our own people.
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'militia').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_militia_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'militia');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@commit_both
title: Call both the railway workers and the Milicja
choose-if: {! return PolishSecurity.coupCommitStatus(Q, 'both').available !}
unavailable-subtitle: [+ pl_coup_both_why +]
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupCommit(Q, 'both');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f67
