Who answered the call: [+ pl_coup_called +].

The army groups, one draw each: [+ pl_coup_sides +].

Arrivals: [+ pl_coup_arrivals +].

[+ pl_coup_rounds +].

- @f67_seen: Continue.

@f67_seen
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupStepSeen(Q, 'f67');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f9
new-page: true

= An offer of settlement

The Marshal of the Sejm presents a settlement: [+ pl_coup_f9 +]. Every settlement also returns the troops to their garrisons, gives an amnesty without repression of the participants, keeps the Sejm and the calendar of elections, and ends the mobilisation of PPS. Because our share in the fighting is significant, the settlement needs our voice. If we reject it, no settlement is possible until the end of this attempt, also in the final assessment; the rejection breaks no agreement and does not change our reputation.

- @f9_accept
- @f9_reject

@f9_accept
title: Support the settlement
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupF9(Q, 'accept');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f9_reject
title: Reject it and keep our organisations engaged
on-arrival: {!
PolishSecurity.coupF9(Q, 'reject');
!}
go-to: polish_event_coup

@f10
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
// 19.1: the resolved attempt ends the chapter; the report is recorded once.
PolishInstitutions.endChapterIfDue(Q);
!}

